222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (The Pears Project proposal had the ambitious goal of exploring and implementing new volunteer roles within Home-Start Nottingham, while also establishing a stronger presence within the community, both online and in person. We explored the development of social media, admin, and translator volunteer roles, while building upon the existing events, fundraising, and group volunteer model. We also focused on engaging with the community, connecting with other charities and partner agencies, and broadening our visibility online.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Some of the positive outcomes include the successful recruitment of a dedicated and active admin volunteer, alongside the creation of an admin volunteer role template that can continue to be implemented in the future. We now also have a regular newsletter, run by one of our social media volunteers, which aims to add value to the overall volunteer experience.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (In addition, we have developed a pool of 11 events volunteers after trialling the events volunteer role as an ad hoc opportunity for home-visiting volunteers. The more volunteer support we have, the more events we are able to attend, with the long-term aim of eventually having some events run entirely by volunteers. Moving forward, we are also exploring the possibility of creating a Vinted volunteer role under the fundraising umbrella to assess whether this could provide a more regular source of fundraising income.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Following further consideration, we made the decision to discontinue the translator volunteer role due to the complexity of matching volunteers with the appropriate families, alongside the level of training required. Social media volunteers continue to be an area we believe could add significant value; however, we are currently re-evaluating how the role could be structured to make it more accessible and sustainable.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Overall, the project has produced many positive outcomes, alongside some unexpected learning opportunities. While there is still work to do in order to fully maximise the remaining project timeframe, the progress made so far has provided a strong foundation for future development.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
